WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.241 --> 00:00:06.296
Hello, my name is Taha Jaid, SOC Manager at AMANDIGITAL,

2
00:00:06.847 --> 00:00:09.399
a SOC provider, an MSSP.

3
00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:14.924
About your topic: in my work at AMANDIGITAL, since I started,

4
00:00:15.435 --> 00:00:16.956
where I’m now SOC Manager,

5
00:00:16.996 --> 00:00:21.470
I handle all the architecture and configuration of our SOC.

6
00:00:22.261 --> 00:00:26.285
I’ve had the chance to take part in recruiting young cybersecurity profiles,

7
00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:30.178
especially final-year interns, and even end-of-year interns.

8
00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:35.714
What I learned from this experience is that a candidate who aces the interview

9
00:00:35.754 --> 00:00:39.027
isn’t necessarily the most competent one in the field.

10
00:00:40.018 --> 00:00:42.080
Some are very at ease speaking,

11
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.493
while others are more reserved because of stress.

12
00:00:46.144 --> 00:00:51.068
Personally, I don’t see nervousness as a lack of skills.

13
00:00:51.108 --> 00:00:55.192
What interests me above all is their ability to think, to analyse a problem

14
00:00:55.232 --> 00:00:56.594
and explain their reasoning.

15
00:00:56.634 --> 00:01:00.097
And especially, if they are engineering students,

16
00:01:00.137 --> 00:01:07.624
do they think like an engineer, whose role is to find solutions to problems?

17
00:01:07.664 --> 00:01:10.827
Because I don’t rely much on the technical level;

18
00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:15.521
but above all, I look at how they think, how they reason.

19
00:01:16.072 --> 00:01:18.234
For example, in our field, cybersecurity,

20
00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:23.019
I prefer to present a concrete situation, like a suspicious security alert,

21
00:01:23.059 --> 00:01:27.573
and ask the candidate how they would investigate and handle it.

22
00:01:28.084 --> 00:01:30.966
I’m not necessarily looking for a perfect answer.

23
00:01:31.006 --> 00:01:35.390
Above all, I want to understand their logic, their curiosity, their ability to learn.

24
00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:41.586
And if the alert or the problem was really complicated for them,

25
00:01:43.038 --> 00:01:46.281
I’d like to see that they never give up.

26
00:01:46.321 --> 00:01:50.044
Because in our field, cybersecurity,

27
00:01:50.084 --> 00:01:53.347
if you give up, it’s over: you just switch to another problem

28
00:01:53.387 --> 00:01:55.009
because it’s too complicated.

29
00:01:55.049 --> 00:02:00.134
There are fewer resources online, especially for solving problems or alerts.

30
00:02:00.174 --> 00:02:03.697
And of course, technical knowledge matters too,

31
00:02:03.737 --> 00:02:08.802
but motivation, an analytical mind and the will to improve matter just as much.

32
00:02:08.842 --> 00:02:13.086
And for me, a recruiter’s role is to give every candidate

33
00:02:13.126 --> 00:02:19.342
a real chance to show their potential, without stopping at the first impression.
